.TH mouser-plugin-retry 1  "mouser-plugin-retry 1.4.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mouser\-plugin\-retry \- Queue the failed downloads again (first run, installs, updates)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmouser plugin retry\fR [\fB\-\-kind\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queue the failed downloads again (first run, installs, updates)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-kind\fR \fI<KIND>\fR
Only this kind: mode, engine, model\-provider, tool\-provider, command. With `engine` this is `mouser engine …`
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Install or update without asking (the card\*(Aqs answer is yes)
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
The version to install (a GitHub tag or what the lock pins)
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fR
Wait for the download to finish (the CLI always does; for scripts)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmouser\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v1.4.0
